A||||4||Alex2004||Cannot find trunk relay!!!||||4||
Z||000000||Alex2004||10-20-2001||08:14 PM||||Hi, i've looked under the steering column like everyone says to look and i still cannot find the relay, i have an 84 SE, and i think the relay is bad, but i cannot find it.  How far is it under there, is there anything i need to take off to see it.  And what color is the relay?  Also, is it to the left or right when your looking under the dash on yuor back?  Let me know! Thanks<P>Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||10-20-2001||09:27 PM||||remove the plastic pannel under the steering column for better access. It should be clipped on the right side of the frame member that support the steering column and brake pedal. It looks like the horn relay except I think it's black. (And Yes, a horn relay can be used to test or replace it.)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||10-20-2001||10:02 PM||||Yet another 84 only difference rears its ugly head!  There is no relay in the trunk release system on the 84's.  The circuit is extremly simple.  There is a pink/black wire that brings power from the "gages" fuse to the switch on the dash.  From there, a black wire feeds the trunk release solonoid on the decklid directly.  The other two wires on the switch (gray and smaller diameter black) are for the light bulb in the switch.<BR>As a side note, the ignition switch must be in the "run" position to supply power to the trunk release switch.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trunk_release.jpg">   <BR>Sorry about the large size, but at least it's readable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 10-20-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 10-20-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||SLYGUY||10-21-2001||01:11 AM||||That's strange. <BR>With my 88GT you can't use the decklid power release switch unless the ingniton is OFF. I know it is a safety thing or something, as annoying as it is. So many times you want to look at or take a listen to something after you fire up the motor only to remember that the power decklid release will not work with the ignition in the RUN position. You have to switch the ign. off. <BR>The 84s are different?<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||10-21-2001||12:49 PM||||Yeah, one of several things that were unique to the 84's.  Keeps life interesting <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>On your 88, try your trunk opener with the engine running and the parking brake applied--my 88 will open the trunk under that condition or with the ignition off.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
